NAME
       symlink, readlink - symbolic links

SYNOPSIS
       #include <unistd.h>

       int     symlink(const char *target, const char *path);
       ssize_t readlink(const char *path, char *buf, size_t size);

DESCRIPTION
       symlink creates PATH pointing at TARGET, which need not exist.
       readlink reads the target back without following it, and does
       not terminate the buffer.

       Hard links are not implemented, so a symbolic link is the only
       kind available.

RETURN VALUE
       symlink returns 0; readlink returns the byte count. Both return
       -1 with errno set on failure.

ERRORS
       EEXIST    path already exists
       EINVAL    the path is not a symbolic link

SEE ALSO
       ln(1), stat(2)
